---
/**
 * RemoteSection — landing section for --remote mode.
 *
 * The daemon serves a token-gated, deck-only emulator URL on your LAN.
 * Scan the QR the CLI prints (illustrative QR here) and your phone becomes
 * the deck — no Stream Deck hardware required. The deck mock sits inside a
 * landscape phone frame.
 */
---

<section id="remote" class="px-6 py-24" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14 items-center">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-4"
          style="color: var(--color-accent);"
        >
          Remote mode
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold leading-[1.05] mb-6 text-fg">
          Your deck,<br />in your pocket.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6" style="color: var(--color-muted);">
          No Stream Deck hardware required. Start the daemon with
          <code class="font-mono text-sm px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-surface-raised);">--remote</code>
          and it serves a token-gated, deck-only view on your LAN. Scan the QR
          it prints and your phone becomes the deck.
        </p>

        <div
          class="rounded-lg px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm mb-6 overflow-x-auto"
          style="background: var(--color-bg); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-accent);"
        >
          sireno start --remote
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 mb-8">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 mt-1">
            <i data-lucide="shield-check" class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-accent);"></i>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-muted);">
            The URL is token-gated — only devices with the QR-scoped link can
            connect. Buttons tap straight into the same runtime as hardware.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a
          href="/user/emulator-vs-hardware/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold transition-colors"
          style="color: var(--color-accent);"
        >
          Connectivity &amp; remote docs
          <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="w-4 h-4"></i>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-8" data-reveal>
        <!-- landscape phone frame with the deck inside -->
        <div
          class="relative rounded-[2rem] p-2"
          style="background: var(--color-surface-raised); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); box-shadow: 0 25px 60px -15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); width: min(100%, 460px);"
        >
          <!-- side buttons (landscape) -->
          <span class="absolute -left-[3px] top-1/4 w-[3px] h-8 rounded-l" style="background: var(--color-border);"></span>
          <span class="absolute -left-[3px] top-1/2 w-[3px] h-8 rounded-l" style="background: var(--color-border);"></span>
          <span class="absolute -right-[3px] top-1/3 w-[3px] h-10 rounded-r" style="background: var(--color-border);"></span>
          <div class="rounded-[1.6rem] overflow-hidden" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-border);">
            <img
              src="/captures/01-default.png"
              alt="Sireno Deck running on a phone in remote mode"
              class="w-full block"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <!-- camera punch-hole (landscape: left edge) -->
          <span
            class="absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 left-4 w-2 h-2 rounded-full"
            style="background: var(--color-bg); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
          ></span>
        </div>

        <!-- QR -->
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3 flex-shrink-0">
          <div
            class="rounded-xl p-3"
            style="background: var(--color-bg); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
          >
            <img src="/qr-remote.svg" alt="QR code linking to the Sireno Deck remote emulator" class="w-24 h-24 block" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="text-[0.6875rem] font-mono text-center max-w-[7rem]" style="color: var(--color-muted);">
            scan at runtime for your deck URL
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
